  "description": "OJUSEV crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C85 H78 Dy9 N17 O27 S17,C1 H4 O1,5.75(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.556-5.071 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.14-155.81°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(L)17(μ3-OH)9(μ4-OH)]·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 9 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 9 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
